WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.000
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody!

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.234
You're here.
You made it.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:06.133
Thank you for watching.
Thank you for being here.

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:07.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.868
Guys, we are right in the middle
of the holiday season.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.300
Are you excited?

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:16.200
According to a survey,
during the holidays,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.734
most dog owners
buy a gift for their pet.

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.567
Yeah.
And then there's the people

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.968
that are too lazy to shop
and just give their dog cash.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.100
Buying a gift for a dog
is stressful.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.567
I mean, seriously,
there's nothing more depressing

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:31.067
than watching your dog
open a present

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.701
then fake wagging his tail.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:35.467
You go, "Okay.
He didn't like it. Okay."

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.367
Let's get to some news.
Today, President Biden

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:39.100
hosted a ceremony
on the South Lawn

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.601
to sign a bill that mandates
federal recognition

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.000
for same-sex marriages.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:50.167
Yeah.

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:52.167
When he heard,
Mike Pence was like,

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.133
"Barkeep, give me a shot
of whole milk."

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:56.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.534
"Just leave the whole carton."

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:58.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.434
Yeah, the bill protects
all marriages.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:01.734
Unless you're
one of those couples

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.901
who feed each other in public.
Then you're on your own.

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:06.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:09.200
I read that Ivanka Trump
and Jared Kushner

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.334
cut ties
with former president Trump

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:14.767
because he's "losing value"
and they don't need him anymore.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:17.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.467
Trump's not even upset.

00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:20.801
He's like, "The student
has become the master."

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:22.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:24.367
Things are so rough
in the Trump family,

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.100
even the royal family's like,
"Yikes."

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:29.067
Did you guys see this today?

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:31.167
A bipartisan group of lawmakers
announced a bill

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.968
that would ban TikTok
in the U.S.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:36.200
-[ Person whistles ]

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:40.767
Right now, gen Z is like,
"We ride at dawn."

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:45.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:48.801
Critics of TikTok worry that the
app is giving American secrets

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:50.667
to the Chinese government.

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:52.801
Yeah, pretty scary.
Apparently, China has already

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:54.534
mastered the "Wednesday" dance.

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:58.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:01.734
Meanwhile, get this,
a TikTok-famous plastic surgeon

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:03.934
just had her
medical license suspended

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:07.400
after she was accused
of botched surgeries.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.234
See, that's why I only use
YouTube-famous plastic surgeons.

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:11.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:13.167
When asked for a comment,
she said,

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:14.767
"Look, I don't see them
as botched surgeries.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.400
I look at them as cool filters."

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:20.067
Well, guys, New York City
is experiencing high levels

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:23.067
of COVID, flu, and RSV
in what health officials

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:25.701
are calling a "tridemic."

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:27.634
And Pfizer is promoting
a new booster shot

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:29.634
to protect against it.
Check this out.

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:32.100
-As cases continue to rise,
experts recommend

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:36.000
getting the latest boosters
for COVID, the flu, and RSV.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.601
But as the holidays approach,
we might not all have time

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:39.934
for multiple appointments.

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.234
That's why we're introducing

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:42.734
The Destroyer.

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:44.834
Just one quick jab,
and you're protected from...

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:02.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:05.834
♪♪

00:03:05.834 --> 00:03:09.868
-Wow, indeed!
-Wow!

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:13.467
Multiple injections.
Oh, my goodness.

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:14.968
Firecrotch, unbelievable.

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:17.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:19.200
Hey, I want to say
happy birthday to Bob Barker

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.801
who just turned 99!

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:22.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:26.334
We love you, Bob.

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:28.033
You could tell he hosted
"The Price is Right"

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:29.667
'cause that's the closest
you can come to 100

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:30.734
without going over.

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:33.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:35.701
Switching gears,
Uber Eats released

00:03:35.701 --> 00:03:37.634
its annual Cravings Report,
which revealed

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:40.701
the hottest
food-ordering trends of 2022.

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:41.968
And the trends
were pretty interesting.

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:43.701
For example,
more people requested

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:45.701
celery juice on Wednesdays.

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:49.534
-Oh. Man, see, I always ordered
celery juice on Wednesday.

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:53.300
-Yeah. On Friday, there's
a spike in cannoli orders.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.634
-Wow! I get cannolis, you know,
every Friday, too.

00:03:56.634 --> 00:03:58.300
That's crazy.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.801
-Yeah, well, apparently, orders
of ranch dressing went way down.

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:05.133
-Ha! See, I didn't order
any ranch this year.

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:11.133
-And the big drink craze
was a negroni sbagliato.

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:13.834
-Sbagliato, you say.
Those are good.

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:15.534
The only thing better
is a margarita.

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:17.300
It goes great with a steak.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:18.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:20.567
-It makes sense.
I mean, the most frequently

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:24.567
paired food/drink combo
was steak and margarita.

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.000
-Huh.
[ Ominous music plays ]

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.200
Really?

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.934
W-What about Saturdays?

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:32.701
I got to be the only one
who orders tater tots

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:35.801
and says to hold the --
-Sour cream.

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:37.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.100
Dammit.
-W-What?

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.534
What's wrong, Tariq?

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:43.067
-No, it -- it can't be.

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:45.000
-What?
W-- What is it?

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.167
-No way, n-not me.

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.067
-Say it.
What is it, Tariq?

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:50.200
[ Dramatic music crescendos ]

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.133
-I think I might be
a basic bitch.

00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:53.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:56.234
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:59.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:01.534
[ Laughs ]

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:06.067
[ Applause continues ]

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.801
-Or you're a trendsetter.

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:10.934
-Damn right I am!

00:05:10.934 --> 00:05:13.734
♪ You're the best around ♪

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:16.033
♪ Nothing's gonna ever
keep you down ♪

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:17.934
♪ You're the best around ♪

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.901
-Tariq Trotter, everyone.
Tariq Trotter.

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:21.267
Wow, I was worried.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:23.234
I was worried.

00:05:23.234 --> 00:05:24.601
Whew!

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:27.534
I was worried for a second.

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:29.801
Guys, I heard about --
a new study found that people

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:31.167
who wake up with an alarm clock

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:34.400
are more tired than people
who wake up naturally.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.968
Another reason people who use
an alarm clock are tired --

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:38.133
they have jobs.

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:42.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:45.000
This is wild.
An Olive Garden manager

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.701
was fired
after sending the staff

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:48.734
an aggressive warning
about missing work.

00:05:48.734 --> 00:05:49.868
Listen to this.

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:51.834
-The message from
an Olive Garden manager

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:53.701
in Kansas to employees.

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:05.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:07.501
-Good news, though --
today, she was hired to be

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.234
the head of H.R. at Twitter.

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:10.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.200
Good news.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.000
Yeah, it all works out.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.267
And finally,
we have exactly four shows left

00:06:17.267 --> 00:06:19.200
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.234
for that beloved "Tonight Show"
tradition.

00:06:21.234 --> 00:06:24.167
It's time for
"12 Days of Christmas Sweaters."

00:06:24.167 --> 00:06:25.300
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:27.501
-♪ 12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:06:27.501 --> 00:06:32.501
♪ 4 days left ♪

00:06:32.501 --> 00:06:36.033
-That's right! Every show
between now and Christmas,

00:06:36.033 --> 00:06:38.000
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.200
a boom-bastic Christmas sweater

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.968
from the
Countdown to Christmas Cabinet.

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:46.000
Since there are four shows left,
let's open door number 4.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.067
-Let's do it.

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:48.334
[ Drumroll ]

00:06:48.334 --> 00:06:50.200
-Yep.
Go for it.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.734
Wow!

00:06:51.734 --> 00:06:54.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:56.167
Whoo!

00:06:56.167 --> 00:07:00.067
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:07:00.067 --> 00:07:02.934
Can we dim the lights?

00:07:02.934 --> 00:07:04.400
Yeah.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:08.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:08.501 --> 00:07:10.000
Not bad.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.601
Now let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:07:12.601 --> 00:07:13.968
Everyone look at
your seat number.

00:07:13.968 --> 00:07:15.667
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:17.400
Quest, can I get
a drumroll please?

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:19.634
[ Drumroll ]

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:21.734
Who wants this sweater?
It's a good one!

00:07:21.734 --> 00:07:23.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:26.567
Who's sitting at 430?!

00:07:26.567 --> 00:07:27.834
Yeah!
Come on, bud!

00:07:27.834 --> 00:07:29.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:35.334
♪♪

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:36.567
Hey!

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:39.934
♪♪

00:07:39.934 --> 00:07:42.701
Come on over!
You're over there.

00:07:42.701 --> 00:07:45.267
Nice to see you, brother.
Go over there.

00:07:45.267 --> 00:07:47.234
Hey, what is your name,
and where are you from?

00:07:47.234 --> 00:07:49.133
-Giovanni.
Cincinnati, Ohio.

00:07:49.133 --> 00:07:52.100
-Hey, that's what I'm talking
about -- Cincinnati, Ohio!

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:54.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:55.968
I've been to Cincinnati
when it's cold.

00:07:55.968 --> 00:07:57.634
And, man, oh, man,
nothing like having

00:07:57.634 --> 00:07:59.934
the pasta with chili on it,
right?

00:07:59.934 --> 00:08:01.934
-Skyline.
-Yeah, Skyline, exactly.

00:08:01.934 --> 00:08:03.767
And I go there,
and I have to wear a sweater

00:08:03.767 --> 00:08:05.767
'cause it's so cold.
Do you have a sweater like this?

00:08:05.767 --> 00:08:07.234
-I do not.
-Yeah.

00:08:07.234 --> 00:08:08.634
Now you do.

00:08:08.634 --> 00:08:09.801
Would you like to try it on
for everyone?

00:08:09.801 --> 00:08:10.934
-I would love to.
-Here you go, bud.

00:08:10.934 --> 00:08:11.934
Congratulations.

00:08:11.934 --> 00:08:14.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:14.634 --> 00:08:16.968
This will be perfect.

00:08:16.968 --> 00:08:18.300
Go to Skyline -- look at this.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:19.734
Wow.

00:08:19.734 --> 00:08:22.167
Yep.
Oh, my gosh, it's subtle.

00:08:22.167 --> 00:08:24.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's so good.

00:08:24.234 --> 00:08:25.367
It looks good.
Look at you.

00:08:25.367 --> 00:08:27.334
Come on, look at him.

00:08:27.334 --> 00:08:28.434
That's what
I'm talking about, man.

00:08:28.434 --> 00:08:29.434
It looks great.

00:08:29.434 --> 00:08:30.934
Thank you so much.
Congratulations.

00:08:30.934 --> 00:08:32.634
Give it up
for our winner right there.

00:08:32.634 --> 00:08:34.300
Round of applause.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:35.501
Thank you very much.

00:08:35.501 --> 00:08:36.567
She'll take you
to your seat over there.

00:08:36.567 --> 00:08:37.601
Thank you.

00:08:37.601 --> 00:08:38.801
♪♪

00:08:38.801 --> 00:08:40.501
Oh, that's awesome.
Fantastic.

00:08:40.501 --> 00:08:43.033
Hey, you know what?

00:08:43.033 --> 00:08:45.000
You know what?
I'm in the giving spirit.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.334
[ Cheers ]

00:08:46.334 --> 00:08:49.734
I mean, why -- why does
just one person get a gift?

00:08:49.734 --> 00:08:51.601
Why can't everyone
in the audience get a gift?

00:08:51.601 --> 00:08:55.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:57.501
That's right.

00:08:57.501 --> 00:08:59.601
It's time for "Tonight Show
Stocking Stuffers"!

00:08:59.601 --> 00:09:01.200
Here we go!

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.567
-♪ It's the Tonight Show ♪
-♪ Stocking Stuffers ♪

00:09:03.634 --> 00:09:06.234
-♪ It's the Tonight Show ♪
-♪ Stocking Stuffers ♪

00:09:06.234 --> 00:09:09.167
♪ Stocking Stuffers ♪

00:09:09.167 --> 00:09:10.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:10.567 --> 00:09:12.901
-I'm gonna need some help
on this giveaway.

00:09:12.901 --> 00:09:16.400
She is the host of the hit show
"The Drew Barrymore Show."

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:19.434
Ladies and gentlemen,
Drew Barrymore!

00:09:19.434 --> 00:09:21.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:21.234 --> 00:09:23.901
♪♪

00:09:23.901 --> 00:09:25.834
-Hi, guys!

00:09:25.834 --> 00:09:29.200
-Oh! Oh, la la!

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:32.133
[ Both laugh ]

00:09:32.133 --> 00:09:34.801
Oh, look at -- oh, my.

00:09:34.801 --> 00:09:37.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
That is --

00:09:37.334 --> 00:09:40.200
-Oh, look at everybody!

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.234
-Come on, they love you.

00:09:42.234 --> 00:09:44.167
Drew!
Drew!

00:09:44.167 --> 00:09:46.167
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:09:46.167 --> 00:09:48.434
Drew, thank you so much.
-Hi!

00:09:48.434 --> 00:09:49.601
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:09:49.601 --> 00:09:51.434
-Oh, you all look so lovely!

00:09:51.434 --> 00:09:55.133
-They look good, right?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:55.133 --> 00:09:56.534
They're happy you're here.

00:09:56.534 --> 00:09:58.901
-Oh, I'm so happy
to see you guys.

00:09:58.901 --> 00:10:00.267
Happy holidays!

00:10:00.267 --> 00:10:02.100
-Happy holidays, that's right.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:03.501 --> 00:10:04.934
Drew, thank you for being here.

00:10:04.934 --> 00:10:06.033
Thank you for being here.

00:10:06.033 --> 00:10:07.534
-Of course, Jimmy.
-Yes.

00:10:07.534 --> 00:10:10.300
We are about to give them
a stocking stuffer tonight.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:14.701
-Well, I actually hope that
your stocking is very large

00:10:14.701 --> 00:10:18.167
and capable of being stuffed
with the item that I have.

00:10:18.167 --> 00:10:19.467
-Wow!

00:10:19.467 --> 00:10:21.300
[ Laughter ]

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:23.067
Wow.
Wow!

00:10:23.067 --> 00:10:25.334
♪♪

00:10:25.334 --> 00:10:26.567
I-I-I understand.

00:10:26.567 --> 00:10:27.968
That's unbelievable.
Wow.

00:10:27.968 --> 00:10:30.901
-I'm just saying it might be
bigger than a stocking.

00:10:30.901 --> 00:10:32.868
-Okay, all right.
Hey.

00:10:32.868 --> 00:10:34.701
Everyone in tonight's
studio audience

00:10:34.701 --> 00:10:36.200
is going home with this tonight.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:37.567
So no need
to check under your seat.

00:10:37.567 --> 00:10:39.067
Everyone's getting it.
-That's right.

00:10:39.067 --> 00:10:42.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
Everyone is getting it.

00:10:42.367 --> 00:10:44.934
-Tonight, you're all
going home with...

00:10:44.934 --> 00:10:48.133
a new beautiful
